{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1489540-scale-in-combat","id":1489540,"title":"Scale in combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-09T03:18:48-07:00","id":1489540,"title":"Scale in combat","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So I\u2019m running my first game in this new system and I want to make sure I\u2019m running this as intended, so I wanted to check on how to apply scale in combat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example 1: Powerful Nova attacking baseline.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A nova with mega-might 5 attacks a baseline. The attacker has scale 5 on attack, the defender has scale 1 on defense. So the Nova rolls Might+Close Combat to hit the baseline. If they beat the target\u2019s defense they then get to say what happens to the baseline (since more than 3 levels gets to dictate the outcome) or does that mean they don\u2019t even need to roll to hit? </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example 2: Less-powerful nova attacking baseline.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So say that Nova only has Mega-might 3, then would their attack roll be Might+Close combat to hit and if they hit they get a level 6 enhancement (for having a scale 3 higher)?</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T03:38:10-07:00","id":1489541,"title":"","content":"Example 1: If it\u2019s such a minor challenge don\u2019t need to roll.<br /> Example 2: Yes, that is the idea.<br /> <br /> But my suggestion for you is scale from Mega-Might (and other sources of scale) only apply to damage (stunts that cause injuries), and not to hit (beat defense), so if the baseline have high defense they scape the attack, but if not they are instantly killed with many injuries.<br /> Think a fly and you and how hard it is to hit it, but if you hit it\u2019s dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-09-2022, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T05:41:49-07:00","id":1489546,"title":"","content":"Your math is a little off. Mega-Might adds to your base Scale, not replaces it. So the MM5 Nova would have 6 Scale on the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T10:59:53-07:00","id":1489568,"title":"","content":"I think Mateus is right based on how Mega-Might is worded. They kinda bent over backwards in the Mega-Att write-ups to keep them from giving Scale to all rolls made with that Attribute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Increase might Scale by their Mega-Might dots for lifting and moving, and power Scale for damaging things using sheer muscle power. </div> </div> </div>I don't think Mega-Might would give any Scale for trying to hit someone, but once you have you'd have a ton of enhancement for stunts related to &quot;damaging things using sheer muscle power&quot; so you'd be able to buy Inflict Damage multiple times, and have a bunch of enhancement for dealing with Soft Armor and buying the Critical and Sunder stunts.<br /> <br /> In terms of &quot;what happens due to the difference in Scale&quot; the person being hit is just Taken Out, which is also what happens if you don't just hand wave it due to scale differences. For your example the nova would have 5 scale difference between them and the baseline, so they can buy the Inflict Damage stunt 5 times (or is it five extra times for a total of 6), and have 10e hanging around to deal with Soft Armor and buy the Critical stunt for another level of damage. So like 6 or 7 levels of damage should run through the Health of almost any Antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T01:30:09-07:00","id":1489614,"title":"","content":"Whoops, you are correct that Mega Might 5 would be scale 6. And yeah I have been running it as a bonus to hit but to attack...which is a bit weird mechanically since damage isn't a thing that is rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T03:02:14-07:00","id":1489617,"title":"","content":"Roll standard Close Combat + Might. If you overcome Defense and hit the opponent, then apply Might Scale for working out damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T11:10:50-07:00","id":1490724,"title":"","content":"Of note, Might Scale only adds Enhancement for purchasing the Inflict Damage stunt, so your dice successes get you general enhancement, but if you don't get enough successes to hit, ope.<br /> <br /> Also, Might Scale over Durability (or arguably Size) gets you the ability to purchase additional Inflict Damage stunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 08-19-2022, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}